===Etymology 2===
From {{inh|ang|gem-pro|*gabalō||fork}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|ang}} {{m|ine-pro|*gʰabʰ-||boar-spear, fork, groin}}. Cognate with {{cog|osx|gavala}}, {{m|osx|gaflia||fork}}, {{cog|goh|gabala||twi-pronged or multi-pronged fork}}, {{cog|nl|gaffel}}, {{m|nl|gavel||fork}}, {{cog|de|Gabel||fork}}, {{cog|sga|gabul||fork, forked branch}}. More at {{l|en|gaffle}}.

